# Agents Must Follow Cursor Rules

Sub-agents launched via Task tool start with FRESH context and do NOT automatically
inherit the parent's always-apply rules.

When launching ANY sub-agent (Task tool, generalPurpose, explore, shell, fast):
1. ALWAYS include at the TOP of the prompt: "Follow all workspace cursor rules in .cursorrules"
2. ALWAYS remind: "See no-summary-docs.mdc for documentation rules; plans only in unified-trading-pm or unified-trading-pm/plans/ai/"
3. ALWAYS remind: "uv not pip, basedpyright not pyright, quickmerge not git push"
4. ALWAYS remind: "Delete deprecated code; no parallel code paths — see delete-deprecated.mdc"
5. ALWAYS remind: "Search unified libraries before implementing anything new"

For multi-step agents: put the rule reminder at the TOP of the prompt, not buried at the end.

